        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T21:12:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`bitness` is basically an [alias of `ArchType.Multilib`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/android/arch.go;drc\u003db9c67e21ac0b240af8219d881f95860969a695c8;l\u003d141). \n\n\u003e Is it possible for multilib to be \"32\" but for both \"32\" and \"64\" to be in `bitness`?\n\nI\u0027m not sure if this scenario is possible, but I think the opposite can be possible (e.g. multilib is \"both\", but `bitness` contains either \"32\" or \"64\", not both).",
      "parentUuid": "8071b125_45d576b3",
      "revId": "f4eb421aa2e3b5c375504006facc30f761e60519",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
